  m_Name: nat-traversal
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: GameTerms.Runtime::GameTerms.GlossaryTermAsset
  data:
    Id: nat-traversal
    Term: NAT Traversal
    Abbreviation: nat
    Category: 5
    Difficulty: 2
    ShortDefinition: Techniques that help peers connect through home routers and
      network address translation.
    SimpleExplanation: Helping two phones or PCs find each other even behind routers.
    WhyItMatters: Traversal failures are a common cause of join errors in peer-hosted
      games.
    Example: STUN or relay fallback lets two mobile players connect successfully.
    CommonMistake: Assuming all players can host without providing a relay option.
    PracticePrompt: 'Document a connection path: direct, STUN, then TURN relay fallback.'
    GameUses:
    - Peer-to-peer games
    - Mobile multiplayer
    - Co-op hosting
    RelatedTermIds:
    - dedicated-server
    - packet-loss
    - matchmaking
    Tags:
    - networking
    - connectivity
    - mobile
    Synonyms: []
